Cobalt(III) forms two isomeric octahedral complexes with the formula $[\text{Co}(\text{NH}_3)_3(\text{NO}_2)_3]$. The $\text{NO}_2^-$ ion is monodentate.

Complete the diagrams to show the three-dimensional structures of the two isomers and suggest the type of isomerism shown here.

